From 7b50a5cebf09fb36c4fdb322a0d0b10b44bbbd63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld
 <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:00:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: platform_profile: fix uninitialized return
 in pm_prepare

surface_platform_profile_pm_prepare() declares "int status;" without an
initializer and only assigns it inside the "if (tpd->has_fan)" block.
On devices where the "has_fan" property is not set, such as the Surface
Pro 7 and the Surface Book 3, the function returns whatever happens to be
on the stack. Any non-zero value makes the PM core abort the transition:

  surface_platform_profile 01:03:01:00:01: PM: device_prepare():
    surface_platform_profile_pm_prepare [surface_platform_profile]
    returns -1050009088
  surface_platform_profile 01:03:01:00:01: PM: not prepared for power
    transition: code -1050009088
  PM: Some devices failed to suspend, or early wake event detected

and the machine immediately resumes instead of suspending.

Initialize status to 0 so that devices without a fan report success.

Fixes: 743c726b18f6 ("platform/surface: platform_profile: add fan power state handling")
Signed-off-by: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Patchset: surface-sam
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c
index 203d21aa7..38d2c3b23 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_platform_profile.c
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ static int surface_platform_profile_probe(struct ssam_device *sdev)
 static int surface_platform_profile_pm_prepare(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct ssam_platform_profile_device *tpd;
-	int status;
+	int status = 0;
 
 	tpd = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-- 
