From 212cfbd0ba2fe42d437bc04535f2768d35b76eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld
 <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:04:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Add thermal sensors
 and fan speed for Surface Book 3

The Surface Book 3 EC provides the same thermal sensor (TMP, function 2)
and fan speed (FAN, instance 1) interfaces as the newer devices that
already list them, but the Surface Book 3 node group does not include
them. Add both nodes so that surface_temp and surface_fan can bind.

Tested on a Surface Book 3 (15", i7-1065G7) by registering the same two
nodes from an out-of-tree module: surface_temp exposes the nine EC
sensors (I_RTS1 to I_RTS8 and I_VTS1, names reported by the EC) and
surface_fan reports the fan speed. The values match the raw EC readings
obtained through the SSAM cdev.

The fan maximum already follows the platform profile on this device
(about 6000 to 8000 rpm from low-power to performance), so keep the
platform profile node without the has_fan property.

The analysis, the out-of-tree test module and this changelog were
prepared with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude, Anthropic).
I reviewed the change and tested it on the device as described above.

Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/kernel/issues/117
Signed-off-by: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Patchset: surface-sam
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index ef87965fc..ce1ffd283 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -241,6 +241,8 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sb3[] = {
 	&ssam_node_bat_main,
 	&ssam_node_bat_sb3base,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_perf_profile,
+	&ssam_node_tmp_sensors,
+	&ssam_node_fan_speed,
 	&ssam_node_bas_dtx,
 	&ssam_node_hid_base_keyboard,
 	&ssam_node_hid_base_touchpad,
-- 
