From 147e7fac8cc79ce625019c9e86ec20e4701f2a30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld
 <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:33:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: surface_temp: Add support for the KIP thermal sensors

On the Surface Book 3, the base (keyboard and peripheral controller, KIP)
has its own set of thermal sensors behind the same TMP interface as the
ones on the main controller (SAM). Add a match entry for the KIP target
so that the driver can bind to such a node.

Devices only get a TMP node on the KIP target if the registry lists one
for them, so this does not change anything for other devices.

Tested on a Surface Book 3 (15", i7-1065G7) with the registry node from
the next patch, registered from an out-of-tree module: the driver binds
and exposes the nine base sensors (I_RTS1 to I_RTS8 and I_VTS1, names
reported by the EC).

The analysis, the out-of-tree test module and this changelog were
prepared with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude, Anthropic).
I reviewed the change and tested it on the device as described above.

Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/kernel/issues/117
Signed-off-by: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Patchset: surface-sam
---
 drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c b/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c
index cd21f331f..ba51c567a 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c
@@ -216,6 +216,7 @@ static int ssam_temp_probe(struct ssam_device *sdev)
 
 static const struct ssam_device_id ssam_temp_match[] = {
 	{ SSAM_SDEV(TMP, SAM, 0x00, 0x02) },
+	{ SSAM_SDEV(TMP, KIP, 0x00, 0x02) },
 	{ },
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(ssam, ssam_temp_match);
-- 
