From 3746afcedaefe81d08379404e81bbe7fe62bd899 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld
 <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:33:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Add base thermal
 sensors for Surface Book 3

The Surface Book 3 base provides a second set of thermal sensors on the
KIP target. Add the node below the base hub, like the other base
devices, so that it is removed when the clipboard is detached and added
again on attach, and so that surface_temp can bind to it.

On Windows, the skin temperature of the base (I_VTS1 on KIP) is the
input of the power management loop that limits the dGPU.

Tested on a Surface Book 3 (15", i7-1065G7) by registering the same node
below the base hub from an out-of-tree module, together with the
surface_temp match entry from the previous patch: a second
surface_thermal hwmon device appears with the nine base sensors. Both
hwmon devices report the same sensor names, as provided by the EC; they
can be told apart by their device path.

The analysis, the out-of-tree test module and this changelog were
prepared with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude, Anthropic).
