 <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:15:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: surface_fan: Add support for the KIP fans

The Surface Book 3 base (keyboard and peripheral controller, KIP) has
two fans of its own, with the same FAN interface as the fan on the main
controller (SAM), on instances 1 and 2. Add match entries for them so
that the driver can bind to such nodes.

Devices only get FAN nodes on the KIP target if the registry lists them,
so this does not change anything for other devices.

Tested on a Surface Book 3 (15", i7-1065G7) with the registry nodes from
the next patch, registered from an out-of-tree module: the driver binds
to both base fans. They report 0 rpm at idle; under dGPU load, the raw
EC readings through the SSAM cdev showed both fans at about 2700 rpm
after roughly two minutes.

The analysis, the out-of-tree test module and this changelog were
prepared with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude, Anthropic).
I reviewed the change and tested it on the device as described above.

Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/kernel/issues/117
Signed-off-by: Lars Schellhas van Kisfeld <lars.schellhas-van-kisfeld@schellhasconsulting.de>
Patchset: surface-sam
---
 drivers/hwmon/surface_fan.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/surface_fan.c b/drivers/hwmon/surface_fan.c
index aafb4ac92..5fb18ae6c 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/surface_fan.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/surface_fan.c
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@ static int surface_fan_probe(struct ssam_device *sdev)
 
 static const struct ssam_device_id ssam_fan_match[] = {
 	{ SSAM_SDEV(FAN, SAM, 0x01, 0x01) },
+	{ SSAM_SDEV(FAN, KIP, 0x01, 0x01) },
+	{ SSAM_SDEV(FAN, KIP, 0x02, 0x01) },
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(ssam, ssam_fan_match);
