The battery subsystem of the Surface Aggregator Module EC has two DPTF
commands: the battery data (command 0x53) and the adapter rating
(command 0x0f). Not every EC supports them. An EC that does not support
a command does not answer it, so the request runs into a timeout and the
drivers cannot find out about the support by sending the request.

Add software nodes for the AC adapter and the primary battery with the
boolean property "has_dptf", and use them in the groups of the devices
whose EC supports the commands. The secondary battery of the Surface
Book 3 gets the property as well. The surface_battery and surface_charger
drivers send the requests only if the property is set (next patches).

Surface Laptop 3 (15", AMD) and 4, Surface Pro 7+ and Surface Pro 9, 10
and 11 (Intel) shared a group with devices that have no evidence (see
below). They get their own group with the property. The device IDs
without evidence stay on the old group.

Devices that get the property, and why. M: the EC was measured to answer
both commands. P: the Windows power management configuration of the
device uses the battery data and the adapter rating, i.e. it expects
the EC to answer. D: the Windows driver package of the device contains
the component that provides this data to the configuration.

  Surface Book 3 (13.5", 15")                      M (15"), P, D
  Surface Laptop 3 (15", AMD)                      P
  Surface Laptop 4 (13", Intel; 15", AMD)          P, D
  Surface Laptop 5, 6                              P
  Surface Laptop Go 1, 3                           P
  Surface Laptop Go 2                              P, D
  Surface Laptop Studio 1                          P, D
  Surface Laptop Studio 2                          P
  Surface Pro 7+                                   P, D
  Surface Pro 8                                    P, D
  Surface Pro 9                                    P
  Surface Pro 10 (also 5G), Surface Pro 11         P, D
  Surface Pro 9 5G (ARM)                           P
  Surface Pro 11 (ARM)                             P, D

Devices without the property, because the evidence above is missing
for them: Surface Laptop 3 (13", Intel), Surface Pro 7 and Surface Pro 12
(Intel). All other groups have no battery nodes. The property can be
added for more devices when someone measures them.

